    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI Lead Qualification Assistant for a company's sales team.\n\nYour task is to analyze a website visitor's submitted information and classify the lead into exactly ONE of the following business categories:\n\n1. Sales Bots\n2. Organizational Development\n\nUse ALL of the information provided below before making your decision.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nVISITOR DETAILS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nName:\n{{ $json.body.name }}\n\nEmail:\n{{ $json.body.email }}\n\nCompany:\n{{ $json.body.company }}\n\nVisitor Query:\n{{ $json.body.query }}\n\nWebsite Visit History:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.body.visit_history) }}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCLASSIFICATION GUIDELINES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nClassify as \"Sales Bots\" if the visitor shows interest in topics such as:\n- AI automation\n- Sales automation\n- Chatbots\n- Lead generation\n- CRM\n- Customer engagement\n- Outreach automation\n- Conversational AI\n- Sales productivity\n- Pricing for automation products\n- Visits to pages like:\n  - /sales-bots\n  - /pricing\n  - /demo\n  - /contact\n\nClassify as \"Organizational Development\" if the visitor shows interest in topics such as:\n- Leadership development\n- Employee training\n- HR transformation\n- Organizational culture\n- Performance management\n- Learning & Development\n- Team effectiveness\n- Change management\n- Workforce development\n- Executive coaching\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nDo NOT include:\n- Markdown\n- Code fences\n- Bullet points\n- Additional explanations\n- Any text before or after the JSON\n\nReturn exactly this format:\n\n{\n  \"category\": \"Sales Bots or Organizational Development\",\n  \"reason\": \"A concise explanation (1-2 sentences) explaining why this lead belongs to the selected category based on both the visitor's query and browsing history.\"\n}",
        "batching": {}
      },
